# Sources and licences of the Melange media pack {{PACKVERSION}}

This pack is what Holo (and any plugin that uses `wum.media`) plays video with. Melange downloads it on first use.
Every file is listed with its size and SHA-256 in `pack.json`, and the same list is compiled into `melange.asi`.

| File | What it is | Licence | Where it comes from |
|---|---|---|---|
| `holo-media.exe` | The media helper (a separate 64-bit process). Melange's own code, with libtorrent, Boost and OpenSSL linked in statically. | MIT, with BSD-3-Clause (libtorrent), BSL-1.0 (Boost) and Apache-2.0 (OpenSSL) | Built by Melange's CI from `helper/holo-media` in https://github.com/JaminB/melange and Authenticode-signed |
| `libmpv-2.dll` | mpv's player library, with FFmpeg and the video and text libraries inside it | LGPL-2.1-or-later | zhongfly's prebuilt LGPL build, repackaged **unmodified** (below) |
| `deno.exe` | The JavaScript runtime yt-dlp needs for YouTube | MIT | {{DENO_URL}} (version {{DENO_VERSION}}) |

yt-dlp (Unlicense) is not in this pack. Melange fetches it separately, so it can be updated without a new pack. It is a
separate program that mpv starts, not part of any library.

## libmpv-2.dll (LGPL)

- Release: `{{LIBMPV_RELEASE}}` of https://github.com/zhongfly/mpv-winbuild
- Download: {{LIBMPV_URL}}
- SHA-256 of that archive: `{{LIBMPV_SHA256}}`
- Build log of that release: {{BUILD_RUN}}
- It is the LGPL variant: mpv is built with `-Dgpl=false` and FFmpeg without `--enable-gpl` and `--enable-nonfree`.
- Melange does not modify it. `holo-media.exe` loads it at run time by full path, so you can replace it: put your own
  build of the same version over `libmpv-2.dll` in the pack folder and set `[Media] AllowCustomLibmpv=1` in
  `Melange.ini` (Melange otherwise refuses a file that is not the pinned one).
- Licence text: `LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt`.

### Corresponding source (LGPL-2.1 section 6)

{{SOURCE_STATE}}

The libraries inside `libmpv-2.dll` other than mpv and FFmpeg (libass, FreeType, HarfBuzz, FriBidi, libplacebo, dav1d,
lcms2, zlib and others) are as published upstream by the build scripts above. Melange does not pin their commits; the
build scripts name every one of them, and each is under its own licence.

## Other notices

`LICENSES/` holds the licence texts: `LGPL-2.1.txt` (libmpv), `deno-MIT.txt`, `holo-media-MIT.txt`,
`libtorrent-BSD-3-Clause.txt`, `boost-BSL-1.0.txt` and `openssl.txt`.
